{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1001559-2e-aggravated-damage-and-armor","id":1001559,"title":"[2E] Aggravated Damage and Armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-10T17:54:44-08:00","id":1001559,"title":"[2E] Aggravated Damage and Armor","content":"I imagine I am just missing something here, or reading too much into it... but what are the rules of aggravated damage and armor? Armor rules on pg94 says that general armor applies to all attacks and reduces the total damage taken. Does this really include Aggravated Damage sources? I ask because of Armor Piercing's affect on Durability and how Agg just ignores Durability?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any insight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T18:17:06-08:00","id":1001568,"title":"","content":"In general (so pulling from a few sources here) Agg damage sources rely on common sense and/or explicit statement on this. Part of the issue is &quot;naturally&quot; Agg, and &quot;bane&quot; Agg. A magical attack that does Agg to everything usually ignores armor. Stabbing a werewolf with a silver blade doesn't ignore armor. This makes sense with the idea that the mystic bolt might not even pass through physical space to be impeded by armor, but the knife only does Agg to the werewolf because of the werewolf's weakness. It has to cut the werewolf to do harm, and isn't going to ignore a sheet of metal in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:01:08-08:00","id":1002319,"title":"","content":"Wow, that makes Agg damage extremely powerful for Spirits and Vampires with Wolf Claws I take it should just be shredding body armors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:24:56-08:00","id":1002355,"title":"","content":"Well yes, though 2e downgraded the availability of Agg significantly (Vampires do lethal with their claws without a Merit and even then only in frenzy for example).<br /> <br /> As well, there's still a significant amount of &quot;apply common sense&quot; that's supposed to be applied here over flat rules. Which basically means one ST could rule that Agg dealing claws don't ignore Armor because they still have to cut through stuff before hitting flesh and some of the damage will by ablated, and another ST could say all &quot;natural&quot; Agg ignores Armor unless explicitly disallowed by the power granting Agg damage. Both have enough evidence to be &quot;right&quot; by the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T14:49:48-08:00","id":1002645,"title":"","content":"Wow, i was not aware of the change to the Vampire rules, that helps a lot actually. My game is Mage-oriented and I wanted to add a Vampire and Werewolf conflicts in the backdrop and was just seeing a massive escalation of damage output (which is how my group always rolls)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T15:04:16-08:00","id":1002651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, aggravated damage is much harder to come by in 2e than it was in 1e. It's mostly reserved for things that exploit a supernatural weakness, or that utterly destroy large portions of tissue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T18:53:00-08:00","id":1002739,"title":"","content":"The new way Mage Armor works in 2e also helps make mages a bit less squishy. Damage output is definitely up in 2e, but Armor is also much more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T00:26:10-08:00","id":1002791,"title":"","content":"Remember that Mage Armors are Reflexive, which means they can be activated at any point of time even outside your turn in response to being attacked. Faster than thought or bullets. <br /> <br /> Other thing about Aggravated damage is that it can destroy limbs if damage it caused is attached to a Tilt. This can be potentially devastating to characters without regeneration. Vampires and other self-regenerating thingies have it easy, as while it takes time and is pain in the ass, they can restore damaged limbs and organs permanently just fine. Mages have it hard, because lasting magic won't give you your hand back, and regrowing it means having to sustain regeneration spell indefinitely; it being dispelled equals to your limb withering away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T03:14:02-08:00","id":1002812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1001559-2e-aggravated-damage-and-armor?p=1002791#post1002791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Mage Armors are Reflexive, which means they can be activated at any point of time even outside your turn in response to being attacked. Faster than thought or bullets.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You need a reason still. So you can't activate armor when you are not aware that you are being attacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:57:11-08:00","id":1003114,"title":"","content":"That's still a lot better than a spell you need to cast, regulating the Mage Armors in 1e to things almost everyone had up and running all the time rather than something to call on when needed. Plus the 2e ones are much more varied in what they do, and being able to switch between them (rather than needing to have multiple ones up ahead of time to cover your gaps) reflexively means you can get your best armor for the attack your facing rather than just hoping you had the right ones up ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:15:20-08:00","id":1003233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1001559-2e-aggravated-damage-and-armor?p=1002651#post1002651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, aggravated damage is much harder to come by in 2e than it was in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>My woodchipper that I suplex people into says otherwise.<br /> <br /> Yes, my characters always have a woodchipper close to hand. Always.<br /> <br /> It's a survival trait, don'tcha know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:18:51-08:00","id":1003236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong